1
00:00:15,814 --> 00:00:18,404
Anyway, just don't worry about it.

2
00:00:20,984 --> 00:00:22,114
Okay.

3
00:00:38,364 --> 00:00:39,464
Kobato.

4
00:00:39,464 --> 00:00:40,954
Y-Yes sir...

5
00:00:41,234 --> 00:00:43,834
With the window open all this time,

6
00:00:44,344 --> 00:00:47,074
even someone as clueless as you
is bound to catch a cold.

7
00:00:47,444 --> 00:00:49,274
But I...

8
00:00:53,284 --> 00:00:54,914
I'm cold!

9
00:00:58,224 --> 00:00:59,624
I'm sorry!

10
00:01:00,954 --> 00:01:03,424
Really, it's still very cold, isn't it?

11
00:01:03,894 --> 00:01:06,914
Yes, it's only the beginning of February, after all.

12
00:01:07,494 --> 00:01:08,834
Speaking of which,

13
00:01:08,834 --> 00:01:13,164
so many of the magazines at the convenience
store had features on chocolate!

14
00:01:15,034 --> 00:01:18,264
I wonder if eating chocolate
makes you feel warm.

15
00:01:18,704 --> 00:01:21,574
No, I think it's because
Valentine's Day is coming up.

16
00:01:23,074 --> 00:01:24,874
Valentine's Day?

17
00:01:30,654 --> 00:01:33,794
Kobato.

18
00:01:33,794 --> 00:01:36,624
Kobato.
Dou sureba iin dakke?

19
00:01:36,624 --> 00:01:41,024
Kobato.
Atarimae no kototte itsumo

20
00:01:41,934 --> 00:01:45,234
Muzukashii na

21
00:01:45,234 --> 00:01:48,004
Ureshii toki waratte

22
00:01:48,004 --> 00:01:52,304
Suki na toki ni utaitai dake

23
00:01:52,874 --> 00:01:55,314
Na no ni

24
00:01:56,614 --> 00:02:00,984
Itsuka negai wa kanau to

25
00:02:01,414 --> 00:02:04,684
Demo "itsuka" tte dore kurai?

26
00:02:04,684 --> 00:02:08,174
Machikirenai yo

27
00:02:08,324 --> 00:02:14,094
123! no aizu de ryoute hirogete

28
00:02:14,094 --> 00:02:19,304
Zenshin ni hikari wo atsumete

29
00:02:19,304 --> 00:02:22,134
Doko ni aru no?

30
00:02:22,134 --> 00:02:25,474
Oshiete, watashi ni dekiru koto

31
00:02:25,474 --> 00:02:28,314
Meippai kizu tsuite

32
00:02:28,314 --> 00:02:31,214
Seiippai hashitte

33
00:02:31,214 --> 00:02:35,184
Nan juu kai koronde naite

34
00:02:35,184 --> 00:02:38,224
Sore de mo mada

35
00:02:38,224 --> 00:02:42,244
Akireru kurai

36
00:02:42,724 --> 00:02:46,884
Ashita wo shinjiteru

37
00:02:55,904 --> 00:02:56,804
Yomogi Kindergarten

38
00:02:56,804 --> 00:03:01,674
...The Travelers.
Yomogi Kindergarten

39
00:03:02,744 --> 00:03:04,544
Fujimoto!

40
00:03:10,724 --> 00:03:13,714
February fourteenth is Valentine's Day, right?!

41
00:03:14,994 --> 00:03:16,354
What about it?

42
00:03:16,624 --> 00:03:19,924
How about a Valentine's Day party
at Yomogi kindergarten?!

43
00:03:21,494 --> 00:03:23,264
Why at the kindergarten?

44
00:03:23,834 --> 00:03:26,064
Don't kindergartens have Valentine parties?

45
00:03:26,504 --> 00:03:30,534
I'm sure some do, but in Japan,
that's a day for giving chocolates.

46
00:03:30,604 --> 00:03:33,594
Yes. It also said so in a book.

47
00:03:33,944 --> 00:03:35,244
So I thought, why not the kindergarten too?

48
00:03:35,844 --> 00:03:37,604
What, the girls give chocolates to the boys?

49
00:03:38,744 --> 00:03:39,714
What?

50
00:03:42,584 --> 00:03:45,414
In Japan, it's the day girls give
chocolates to boys they like.

51
00:03:45,654 --> 00:03:48,594
What?! Is that what Valentine's Day is?

52
00:03:49,094 --> 00:03:51,724
Well, I understand nowadays
some boys give to girls too.

53
00:03:52,124 --> 00:03:54,614
But there really is a lot you
don't know, isn't there?

54
00:03:56,094 --> 00:03:57,654
To people you like...

55
00:04:02,074 --> 00:04:03,434
What is it?

56
00:04:05,344 --> 00:04:07,774
Why don't we give it a try?
A Valentine's Day party!

57
00:04:10,714 --> 00:04:12,184
I mean, Ms. Sayaka...

58
00:04:12,814 --> 00:04:16,644
She seems to be deep in thought again lately.

59
00:04:18,024 --> 00:04:22,514
She's under a lot of stress,
but she pretends not to be.

60
00:04:26,934 --> 00:04:32,304
I thought a Valentine's Day party
would cheer her up a bit.

61
00:04:36,404 --> 00:04:37,564
But that's impossible.

62
00:04:38,244 --> 00:04:42,474
The kindergarten financially can't afford
to be having parties these days.

63
00:04:42,474 --> 00:04:43,674
That's not a problem!

64
00:04:44,344 --> 00:04:47,884
B-Bakery Tirol will give us ingredients!

65
00:04:47,884 --> 00:04:50,154
I went by this morning and
they said that I could work

66
00:04:50,154 --> 00:04:54,084
for the ingredients needed to
make the chocolate!

67
00:04:54,494 --> 00:04:55,994
Woah, calm down a bit.

68
00:04:55,994 --> 00:04:57,364
Y-Yes.

69
00:04:57,364 --> 00:05:00,934
So you're saying that you negotiated
with the bakery to work there

70
00:05:00,934 --> 00:05:03,134
and in return the bakery will
pay us with ingredients

71
00:05:03,134 --> 00:05:06,064
for everyone at the kindergarten
to make chocolate with.

72
00:05:12,004 --> 00:05:14,804
U-Um. Did I say something wrong?

73
00:05:15,374 --> 00:05:19,674
My schedule is full. I might not be
able to help out at the bakery.

74
00:05:20,284 --> 00:05:22,684
And I just booked the evenings to work
late night at a construction site.

75
00:05:22,684 --> 00:05:24,614
Oh, I'll be doing the work!

76
00:05:25,584 --> 00:05:31,024
The owner told me that I could come in to
work for him every day after kindergarten,

77
00:05:31,024 --> 00:05:32,854
until Valentine's Day.

78
00:05:33,294 --> 00:05:34,494
But...

79
00:05:34,494 --> 00:05:35,724
I'll be fine!

80
00:05:35,994 --> 00:05:40,124
I, Kobato, will do my best for Valentine's Day!

81
00:05:40,404 --> 00:05:43,134
Go, go, Kobato! Yah!

82
00:05:47,914 --> 00:05:49,874
Okay then, you go for it.

83
00:06:13,434 --> 00:06:15,804
Kobato wants to have a Valentine's Day
party at the kindergarten?

84
00:06:16,174 --> 00:06:17,134
Yes.

85
00:06:18,944 --> 00:06:21,404
She is such a sweet girl, Kobato.

86
00:06:27,014 --> 00:06:29,544
Bakery Tirol

87
00:06:31,754 --> 00:06:35,694
This Year's Chocolates

88
00:06:37,724 --> 00:06:39,314
Thank you for waiting.

89
00:06:40,064 --> 00:06:41,324
Thank you so much.

90
00:06:42,734 --> 00:06:44,704
Please come again!

91
00:06:47,204 --> 00:06:48,394
Thanks for your help.

92
00:06:48,734 --> 00:06:50,394
Good work.

93
00:06:50,804 --> 00:06:52,464
I've still got lots to do!

94
00:06:52,744 --> 00:06:57,304
Yes, I would like to take you up on it,
but today, it's closing time.

95
00:06:57,484 --> 00:07:00,074
Oh, is it that time already?

96
00:07:00,814 --> 00:07:04,274
Um, um... Is there anything
else I can help you with?

97
00:07:04,624 --> 00:07:08,924
There are two more days before
Valentine's Day. You're doing plenty.

98
00:07:09,294 --> 00:07:12,814
Okay then would you please bring
in the sign from outside?

99
00:07:13,064 --> 00:07:15,254
Yes sir! I'll be right back!

100
00:07:32,914 --> 00:07:34,434
Hey! That hurt!

101
00:07:35,614 --> 00:07:37,954
We keep falling upon the strangest places!

102
00:07:38,054 --> 00:07:39,354
Huh?

103
00:07:39,454 --> 00:07:42,654
Well at least we didn't fall in some place
like the middle of the ocean this time.

104
00:07:42,654 --> 00:07:45,254
Yeah, that just about killed us!

105
00:07:45,664 --> 00:07:47,094
Ioryogi-san?

106
00:07:52,134 --> 00:07:54,494
Huh?

107
00:07:58,674 --> 00:08:02,334
Wow, a girl! This world has people!

108
00:08:02,474 --> 00:08:03,644
Hey!

109
00:08:03,644 --> 00:08:07,414
We don't know yet if this is a world
where white buns like you speak!

110
00:08:07,414 --> 00:08:08,054
Right...

111
00:08:08,054 --> 00:08:08,454
Ioryogi-san?
Right...

112
00:08:08,454 --> 00:08:09,284
Ioryogi-san?

113
00:08:09,284 --> 00:08:10,454
Huh?

114
00:08:10,454 --> 00:08:14,214
Umm... this guy's name is Kurogane.

115
00:08:14,994 --> 00:08:15,994
Huh?

116
00:08:15,994 --> 00:08:17,984
And I'm Fay.

117
00:08:18,064 --> 00:08:21,824
This is Syaoran, and this one over here is...

118
00:08:23,034 --> 00:08:24,434
Huh?

119
00:08:25,564 --> 00:08:27,394
Wh-What is it?

120
00:08:29,174 --> 00:08:30,364
Uh, nothing.

121
00:08:34,644 --> 00:08:36,114
Yes. I see.

122
00:08:36,544 --> 00:08:39,244
Mocona, you can talk. It's okay.

123
00:08:39,444 --> 00:08:41,614
This girl is not one bit surprised.

124
00:08:41,714 --> 00:08:45,884
Sure. That's not the only talking
doll. Ioryogi-san talks too.

125
00:08:46,884 --> 00:08:48,154
Ioryogi-san?

126
00:08:48,154 --> 00:08:49,884
Kobato! Come on!

127
00:08:50,054 --> 00:08:51,924
How long do you plan on staying out here?!

128
00:08:52,264 --> 00:08:54,354
The shop owner's starting to get worried...

129
00:08:54,934 --> 00:08:56,484
Ioryogi-san!

130
00:08:58,734 --> 00:09:00,724
So you're Ioryogi-san!

131
00:09:02,904 --> 00:09:04,874
I'm Mocona. How do you do?

132
00:09:05,944 --> 00:09:09,074
Hey, I know you! You're from
that amusement park!

133
00:09:35,134 --> 00:09:37,164
Are you traveling?

134
00:09:37,374 --> 00:09:38,304
Yeah.

135
00:09:38,304 --> 00:09:39,274
A four person journey?

136
00:09:39,274 --> 00:09:41,074
Three persons and one Mocona!

137
00:09:41,214 --> 00:09:42,214
One Mocona?

138
00:09:42,214 --> 00:09:44,044
That's how you count Moconas.

139
00:09:44,644 --> 00:09:48,244
In that case... Ioryogi-san would
count as one Ioryogi-san?

140
00:09:48,314 --> 00:09:50,754
That's wrong! How could you even think that?!

141
00:09:51,224 --> 00:09:55,824
You were right! Kuro-sama and
Ioryogi-san sound alike!

142
00:09:55,824 --> 00:09:57,384
We do not!

143
00:09:58,094 --> 00:09:58,964
You do.

144
00:09:58,964 --> 00:10:00,154
I think you do.

145
00:10:09,534 --> 00:10:12,504
In this world, Kurogane is small and blue.

146
00:10:12,744 --> 00:10:14,504
Shut up, white bun!

147
00:10:15,114 --> 00:10:16,644
Hey, don't you try to get away from me!

148
00:10:16,644 --> 00:10:18,584
So you're visiting on a trip?
Hey, don't you try to get away from me!

149
00:10:18,584 --> 00:10:20,044
Something like that.
Hey, don't you try to get away from me!

150
00:10:20,044 --> 00:10:20,384
Hey, don't you try to get away from me!

151
00:10:20,384 --> 00:10:22,554
I read in a book that when you're on a journey,
you stay in a number of places.
You can't catch me!

152
00:10:22,554 --> 00:10:24,544
I read in a book that when you're on a journey,
you stay in a number of places.

153
00:10:25,124 --> 00:10:27,054
Have you decided where you're staying tonight?

154
00:10:27,184 --> 00:10:29,384
No, not yet.

155
00:10:29,694 --> 00:10:33,284
It would be nice to have a place to stay.

156
00:10:33,364 --> 00:10:35,294
But we don't have any of this world's money.

157
00:10:35,934 --> 00:10:37,904
You don't have any money?

158
00:10:38,134 --> 00:10:40,504
We have money, but I doubt
that they accept it here.

159
00:10:41,934 --> 00:10:43,634
That's a problem.

160
00:10:44,444 --> 00:10:48,394
Well, but there aren't any girls traveling with us,
so I guess we could camp outside.

161
00:10:48,744 --> 00:10:50,614
I'm a girl!

162
00:10:50,614 --> 00:10:53,484
How do you differentiate your gender? By color?

163
00:10:54,154 --> 00:10:55,084
By cuteness.

164
00:10:55,084 --> 00:10:56,074
Huh?

165
00:10:56,654 --> 00:10:58,814
Um, if you need a place...

166
00:10:59,084 --> 00:11:00,384
Uh...

167
00:11:00,524 --> 00:11:02,714
You're welcome to stay with us!

168
00:11:02,894 --> 00:11:04,384
I knew it.

169
00:11:04,924 --> 00:11:06,694
B-But...

170
00:11:06,694 --> 00:11:09,194
No problem at all! We have a room!

171
00:11:09,194 --> 00:11:11,534
Oh, but we only have one futon!

172
00:11:11,634 --> 00:11:14,474
But we could all bundle up and sleep together!

173
00:11:14,474 --> 00:11:17,304
Oh, but you're not all small.

174
00:11:17,304 --> 00:11:21,444
We can separate the top futon from the bottom
futon and we can cover ourselves with those!

175
00:11:21,444 --> 00:11:24,214
You only have one futon? Then you live alone?

176
00:11:24,214 --> 00:11:26,444
No! I live with Ioryogi-san!

177
00:11:27,144 --> 00:11:28,514
Well then all the more!

178
00:11:28,514 --> 00:11:30,484
It will be fine! Really!

179
00:11:30,484 --> 00:11:33,354
Let's take her up on it. Uh...

180
00:11:33,354 --> 00:11:34,844
I'm Kobato Hanato!

181
00:11:35,054 --> 00:11:36,694
Nice to meet you, Kobato!

182
00:11:36,694 --> 00:11:38,294
Hey! You guys!

183
00:11:38,294 --> 00:11:42,784
Whatever happens, you will protect Kobato.
Right, Ioryogi-san?

184
00:11:44,304 --> 00:11:45,524
You...

185
00:11:47,574 --> 00:11:50,574
Anyway, let's go! To Kobato's house!

186
00:11:50,574 --> 00:11:51,544
Go!

187
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:53,264
Yes, let's go!

188
00:11:54,114 --> 00:11:55,974
Off we go!

189
00:11:57,644 --> 00:11:59,304
Is this really okay?

190
00:11:59,884 --> 00:12:02,314
I'm sure he's got something figured out.

191
00:12:03,354 --> 00:12:04,344
Kuro-tan!

192
00:12:04,824 --> 00:12:06,684
Why do you look so put off?

193
00:12:07,324 --> 00:12:09,794
Oops, I made a mistake!

194
00:12:10,424 --> 00:12:15,624
On second thought, he probably has
nothing figured out! That goofball!

195
00:12:17,364 --> 00:12:19,354
I'm late!

196
00:12:19,634 --> 00:12:21,504
It's the kindergarten's day off today.

197
00:12:21,504 --> 00:12:23,234
I've got to work at Bakery Tirol this morning!

198
00:12:23,234 --> 00:12:24,974
Oh, no! What am I going to do!

199
00:12:24,974 --> 00:12:27,144
Oh no! What shall I do? What shall I do?
We tried to wake you up a number of times.

200
00:12:27,144 --> 00:12:27,474
Oh no! What shall I do? What shall I do?

201
00:12:27,474 --> 00:12:29,274
Oh no! What shall I do? What shall I do?
You were in a deep sleep, Kobato.

202
00:12:29,614 --> 00:12:33,014
Nothing changes with you, does it?
Even with all these people in your room.

203
00:12:33,144 --> 00:12:34,544
I'm sorry!

204
00:12:35,154 --> 00:12:39,814
Um, I'm going out, but please stay if
you wish. Make yourselves at home.

205
00:12:40,624 --> 00:12:43,314
Kobato, you're going to the bakery, right?

206
00:12:43,694 --> 00:12:45,254
Yes! To work!

207
00:12:45,724 --> 00:12:50,564
And, uh... They're going to give you ingredients
to make chocolates for Valentine's Day.

208
00:12:50,564 --> 00:12:51,594
That's right.

209
00:12:52,004 --> 00:12:54,904
In that case, we'll help, too.

210
00:12:55,304 --> 00:12:56,274
Huh?

211
00:12:56,534 --> 00:12:59,264
Great idea! For putting us up last night.

212
00:12:59,644 --> 00:13:01,474
Let's see.

213
00:13:01,914 --> 00:13:04,214
Syaoran, you go with her to the bakery.

214
00:13:04,214 --> 00:13:05,084
What?!

215
00:13:05,084 --> 00:13:06,514
You're good at cooking.

216
00:13:06,514 --> 00:13:10,414
Besides, Kuro-sama just doesn't
fit the image of a cake shop?

217
00:13:10,414 --> 00:13:12,484
Don't even ask me. I refuse.

218
00:13:12,484 --> 00:13:15,624
Kuro-tan and I will work somewhere else.

219
00:13:15,624 --> 00:13:17,054
To get some money.

220
00:13:17,154 --> 00:13:18,184
What?

221
00:13:18,564 --> 00:13:19,794
Mocona will...

222
00:13:19,794 --> 00:13:21,664
I'm staying with Ioryogi-san!

223
00:13:22,664 --> 00:13:23,794
Why's that?

224
00:13:24,064 --> 00:13:25,964
I'm starting to like you.

225
00:13:25,964 --> 00:13:27,664
The feeling's not mutual!

226
00:13:28,334 --> 00:13:31,574
So let's get going. We have
a big day ahead of us.

227
00:13:31,574 --> 00:13:32,904
Yeah!

228
00:13:32,904 --> 00:13:34,874
Come on, Ioryogi-san, yeah!

229
00:13:34,874 --> 00:13:35,714
Ah?

230
00:13:35,714 --> 00:13:37,314
Team work between those that get along.

231
00:13:37,314 --> 00:13:38,444
We don't get along!

232
00:13:38,444 --> 00:13:41,054
Oh Ioryogi-san is jealous because I'm so cute.

233
00:13:41,054 --> 00:13:42,174
I'm not jealous!

234
00:13:45,184 --> 00:13:47,214
Yumi, who's the boy?

235
00:13:47,654 --> 00:13:50,484
Oh, apparently someone Kobato knows.

236
00:13:55,864 --> 00:13:58,694
I'm pretty good at pretending to be a stuffed doll.

237
00:13:58,964 --> 00:14:00,524
Hey, stop talking!

238
00:14:01,204 --> 00:14:05,934
This is awesome! Syaoran, you're
really good with your hands.

239
00:14:06,304 --> 00:14:07,794
It's just a matter of getting used to.

240
00:14:08,074 --> 00:14:11,634
I keep practicing, but I can never
get packaged so nicely.

241
00:14:13,084 --> 00:14:14,674
Don't try to stuff it all in at once.

242
00:14:15,214 --> 00:14:16,844
A bit at a time, like this.

243
00:14:18,024 --> 00:14:20,214
A bit at a time...

244
00:14:24,664 --> 00:14:26,184
I did it!

245
00:14:37,234 --> 00:14:39,264
Don't sing, either!

246
00:14:41,114 --> 00:14:45,474
Syaoran, you people have been
traveling for a long time, right?

247
00:14:46,214 --> 00:14:49,704
Yes, but it's not a journey with a destination.

248
00:14:50,284 --> 00:14:51,774
Is that so?

249
00:14:52,084 --> 00:14:55,454
I guess you could say our destination
is to continue traveling.

250
00:15:03,164 --> 00:15:04,354
Um...

251
00:15:04,434 --> 00:15:07,024
Then it's undecided where you're going?

252
00:15:08,074 --> 00:15:09,734
It would be difficult to decide.

253
00:15:10,944 --> 00:15:14,134
For one thing, we don't know how
long we can stay in one place.

254
00:15:20,584 --> 00:15:21,604
But...

255
00:15:23,314 --> 00:15:25,084
I have someone waiting for me.

256
00:15:27,184 --> 00:15:29,084
Someone waiting for you?

257
00:15:30,494 --> 00:15:34,984
Waiting for me, without ever
knowing when I'll be home next.

258
